    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39735" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pȳgĭsĭăcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυγησιακός</span> (not in use), from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυγή</span>, qs. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to secret buttock-worship</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puellam invitare ad pygisiaca sacra,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to copulation</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. S.
					140</span></i>
			 (al. pygiaca, pygiciaca, in the same signif.).</div>
